From: Daniel Ip <kg4368@yahoo.com.hk>
Date: Sun, 13 Jul 2026 23:45:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: qca8084: configure package (incl. SerDes) in probe
 for cold (consumer) bootloaders

The mainline qca8084 driver programs the switch work mode, EPHY LDO and
package clock tree only in .config_init (qca8084_phy_package_config_init_
once), which runs AFTER the per-PHY probe (qca8084_probe ->
devm_clk_get_enabled + phy reset poll). It also brings up the SerDes/
UNIPHY (qca8084_qxgmii_set_mode, incl. analog calibration) only there.

On reference boards (RDP / TP-Link BE800) U-Boot pre-initialises the
QCA8084, so the per-PHY clock enable and reset poll succeed at probe and
.config_init merely re-applies the config. On consumer boards whose
bootloader does NOT init the switch (e.g. Linksys MBE7000), the chip is
cold at probe: the per-PHY clock enable fails -EBUSY (gephy0_sys_clk
stuck) or, with a GPIO reset, the PHY reset poll times out -110.

Move the chip-level bring-up into qca8084_phy_package_probe_once(),
after the package reset is deasserted and before any per-PHY access:
work mode + EPHY LDO, then the SerDes/UNIPHY QXGMII setup, then the
package clock init. The SerDes step must precede the clock init because
switch_core_clk_src / apb_bridge_clk are sourced from the UNIPHY1
312.5 MHz SerDes output, which does not physically exist until
calibration runs (otherwise package_clock_init()'s clk_set_rate() hangs
the RCG: "nss_cc_switch_core_clk_src: rcg didn't update", apb_bridge
stuck off). This mirrors QSDK, which runs qca_mht_interface_mode_init
(SerDes) before ssdk_mht_gcc_clock_init. All ops are idempotent, so
boards where U-Boot already configured the switch are unaffected.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Ip <kg4368@yahoo.com.hk>
---
--- a/drivers/net/phy/qcom/qca808x.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/qcom/qca808x.c
@@ -1067,7 +1067,7 @@
 	struct qca808x_shared_priv *shared_priv;
 	struct reset_control *rstc;
 	struct device_node *child;
-	int i, ret, clear, set;
+	int i, ret, clear, set, mode;
 	struct clk *clk;
 
 	/* Program the MDIO address of PHY and PCS optionally, the MDIO
@@ -1153,7 +1153,66 @@
 				     "package reset not ready\n");
 
 	/* Deassert PHY package. */
-	return reset_control_deassert(rstc);
+	ret = reset_control_deassert(rstc);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	/*
+	 * Consumer bootloaders (e.g. Linksys MBE7000) leave the QCA8084
+	 * unconfigured after the GPIO reset above, so the per-PHY clock enable
+	 * and phy reset in qca8084_probe() fail (-EBUSY / -110). Program the
+	 * work mode, enable the EPHY LDO and bring up the package clock tree
+	 * here - before any per-PHY access - instead of only in .config_init
+	 * (which runs too late). Idempotent where U-Boot already did this.
+	 */
+	switch (shared_priv->package_mode) {
+	case QCA808X_PCS1_10G_QXGMII_PCS0_UNUNSED:
+		mode = QCA8084_WORK_MODE_QXGMII;
+		break;
+	case QCA808X_PCS1_SGMII_MAC_PCS0_SGMII_MAC:
+		mode = QCA8084_WORK_MODE_SWITCH;
+		break;
+	case QCA808X_PCS1_SGMII_MAC_PCS0_SGMII_PHY:
+		mode = QCA8084_WORK_MODE_SWITCH_PORT4_SGMII;
+		break;
+	default:
+		return -EINVAL;
+	}
+
+	ret = qca8084_mii_modify(phydev, QCA8084_WORK_MODE_CFG,
+				 QCA8084_WORK_MODE_MASK,
+				 FIELD_PREP(QCA8084_WORK_MODE_MASK, mode));
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	/* Enable efuse loading into analog circuit */
+	ret = qca8084_mii_modify(phydev, QCA8084_EPHY_CFG,
+				 QCA8084_EPHY_LDO_EN, 0);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	usleep_range(10000, 11000);
+
+	/*
+	 * Bring up the SerDes/UNIPHY (PCS+XPCS QXGMII mode incl. analog
+	 * calibration) BEFORE the package clock init. switch_core_clk_src /
+	 * apb_bridge_clk clock the switch from the UNIPHY1 312.5 MHz SerDes
+	 * output, which physically does not exist until calibration runs - so
+	 * package_clock_init()'s clk_set_rate(APB_BRIDGE, 312.5M) otherwise
+	 * hangs the RCG ("rcg didn't update", apb_bridge stuck off) on boards
+	 * whose bootloader didn't pre-init the SerDes (e.g. Linksys MBE7000).
+	 * QSDK does the same ordering: qca_mht_interface_mode_init (serdes)
+	 * runs before ssdk_mht_gcc_clock_init. config_init still re-runs
+	 * qca8084_qxgmii_set_mode later; the ops are idempotent.
+	 */
+	if (shared_priv->package_mode == QCA808X_PCS1_10G_QXGMII_PCS0_UNUNSED) {
+		ret = qca8084_qxgmii_set_mode(shared_priv->mdiodev[1],
+					      shared_priv->mdiodev[0]);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+	}
+
+	return qca8084_package_clock_init(shared_priv);
 }
 
 static void qca8084_phy_package_remove_once(struct phy_device *phydev)
